{
  "question": "What did Apollo astronauts actually do on the lunar surface, and what did they bring back?",
  "plan": {
    "sub_questions": [
      "What specific activities did Apollo astronauts perform on the lunar surface during their EVAs (walking, geological sampling, photography, instrument deployment, vehicle traverses)?",
      "What scientific experiments and instruments did astronauts deploy and operate on the Moon?",
      "What types of material and hardware did the missions return to Earth (rock and soil samples, core tubes, experiment hardware, film/data)?",
      "How were samples and returned items collected, documented, packaged, and stowed for return (tools, bags, sample boxes, procedures, loading into the lunar module)?"
    ],
    "phrasings": [
      "What did Apollo astronauts actually do on the lunar surface, and what did they bring back?",
      "Astronauts conducted extravehicular activities on the lunar surface to perform geological field work and station operations.",
      "Astronauts collected and bagged lunar rock and soil samples for return to Earth.",
      "Astronauts deployed and activated surface scientific experiments and instrument packages on the Moon.",
      "Astronauts documented the terrain and sample sites with still photography and motion picture film for scientific study.",
      "Astronauts stowed sample boxes, cores and experiment hardware aboard the lunar module for return to Earth.",
      "On missions equipped with a lunar roving vehicle, astronauts used the rover to extend their traverses and collect samples farther from the landing site."
    ],
    "visual_phrasings": [
      "Crew in pressure suits picking up rocks, using tongs and rock hammers, placing specimens into numbered sample bags and boxes.",
      "Astronauts deploying tripod-mounted experiment packages and instruments on the surface while photographing and taking notes.",
      "Loading sample boxes and equipment into the lunar module (close-up of labelled containers, core tubes and film canisters being secured)."
    ],
    "needs_chronology": true,
    "rationale": "I split the question into distinct retrieval targets\u2014surface activities, deployed experiments, returned materials, and collection/stowage methods\u2014so narration-style search phrases and visible-scene descriptions match how NASA archive clips are framed."
  },
  "answer": {
    "answer": "Apollo crews conducted surface exploration and hands\u2011on geological fieldwork on the Moon, collecting rock and soil samples to bring back to Earth [5][8][2]. The archive shows astronauts doing EVAs, handling and photographing lunar rocks, and carrying specimens off the surface for study on Earth [5][7][2]. Not every Apollo crewmember landed \u2014 for example, Michael Collins is remembered in the Apollo context as the crewmember who remained off\u2011surface while others worked on the Moon [4]. Together these clips imply a programmatic focus on surface exploration and sample return rather than only orbital observation, though the clips do not by themselves list specific instruments or the number of samples returned [2][8].",
    "citations": [
      5,
      8,
      2,
      7,
      4
    ],
    "chronology": [
      {
        "citations": [
          5,
          2,
          4
        ],
        "claim": "Archive footage from the Apollo era documents astronauts conducting lunar surface EVAs and collecting samples that were returned to Earth.",
        "era": 1969
      }
    ],
    "caveats": "The clips lack full transcripts and do not establish precise inventories (how many or which samples, or every instrument deployed). Some era labels in the archive are assigned from the video era axis (for example items [5] and [8]), so those dates are based on the archive's video-era tagging rather than independent documentation."
  },
